==Buy Phase==
===Match Start===
*{{AC|TejoMatchStart1.mp3}} "Dropships, artillery, SOPs. Just your typical retirement."
*{{AC|TejoMatchStart2.mp3}} "If they get in my way, I shoot them. If they die, well, they have only themselves to blame."
*{{AC|TejoMatchStart3.mp3}} "My father used to say: the fight is won before the first punch is thrown. We've trained, we are ready, and now, we win."
*{{AC|TejoMatchStart4.mp3}} "This is no little game of banquitas. Focus, or we carry you home in a body bag."
**(''Banquitas'': Benches)
*{{AC|TejoMatchStart5.mp3}} "You know, I had a dream last night. We killed all of them and none of us died. I take it as a sign."

====Attacking====
*{{AC|TejoMatchStartAttack1.mp3}} "If they came here to steal from us, I'd be upset too. I'm still going to kill them, but I understand."
*{{AC|TejoMatchStartAttack2.mp3}} "We take their radianite one way or another."

====Defending====
*{{AC|TejoMatchStartDefense1.mp3}} "The nerve, they come here acting like they own the place. Cómo Pedro por su casa.
**(''Cómo Pedro por su casa'': Like Pedro in his own house (literal), meaning as if they own the place.)
*{{AC|TejoMatchStartDefense2.mp3}} "You think they came here peacefully? No. Let that clear your conscience."

====[[Sunset]]====
*{{AC|TejoMatchStartSunset.mp3}} "Ole, you hear the radio? If anyone finds it, change the station. My team is playing."

===Round Start===
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart1.mp3}} "Do what you're here to do and we won't have a problem."
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart2.mp3}} "If they think it is more honorable to resist death, they're welcome to try."
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart3.mp3}} "Killing them is easier than all this radianite business."
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart4.mp3}} "Make peace with yourself before you pull the trigger. No one else can judge you."
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart5.mp3}} "My ballistic set up easy kills, and if they don't, pues, you can't complain if you're dead."
**(''Pues'': Well)
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart6.mp3}} "No den papaya. If you compromise your position, you hand them a free kill. Don't."
**(''No den papaya'': Don't give away your papaya (literal), meaning to not put yourself in a vulnerable situation.)
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart7.mp3}} "Remember, I hit them with explosives, then you go in. No la vayan a cagar."
**(''No la vayan a cagar'': Don't go screw it up)
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart8.mp3}} "Remember, no one wants to die out here, but you don't always get what you want."
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart9.mp3}} "This should be simple enough. I flush them out, you finish them."
*{{AC|TejoRoundStart10.mp3}} "We can stand around all day talking about killing them, or we just do it."

====Last round won====
*{{AC|TejoRoundWon1.mp3}} "Don't let a good fight go to your head, sure is way to lose it."
*{{AC|TejoRoundWon2.mp3}} "If they don't like losing, they should do something about it."
*{{AC|TejoRoundWon3.mp3}} "Keep it up, hermanos."
**(''Hermanos'': Siblings)
*{{AC|TejoRoundWon4.mp3}} "Okay! Now we do that some more."

=====While in the lead=====
*{{AC|TejoLead1.mp3}} "I'm used to difficult work, this is not so difficult."
*{{AC|TejoLead2.mp3}} "Nothing is guaranteed in war, but I like our odds."
*{{AC|TejoLead3.mp3}} "You think they're worried? I think they're worried."

=====Making a comeback=====
*{{AC|TejoComeback1.mp3}} "Keep pushing. Tenemos mucho camello."
**(''Tenemos mucho camello'': We have a lot of work)
*{{AC|TejoComeback2.mp3}} "That shook their confidence."

